  "bodyTypst": "Let $f$ be a function with derivatives of all orders and for which $f(2)= 7$. When $n$ is odd, the $n$th derivative of $f$ at $x = 2$ is 0. When $n$ is even and $n >= 2$, the $n$th derivative of $f$ at $x = 2$ is given by $f^((n))(2)= frac((n - 1)!,3^(n))$.\n\n(a) Write the sixth-degree Taylor polynomial for $f$ about $x = 2$.\n\n(b) In the Taylor series for $f$ about $x = 2$, what is the coefficient of $(x - 2)^(2 n)$ for $n >= 1$ ?\n\n(c) Find the interval of convergence of the Taylor series for $f$ about $x = 2$. Show the work that leads to your answer.",
